  "id": "neglect",
  "term": "neglect",
  "definition": "Visual neglect is a condition that can follow damage to the right side of the brain, in which a person tends to miss visual information on one side of space. It may be obvious or subtle, and can become more noticeable when attention is divided or task demands are high.",
